summary:
  A settle round killed by its gates keeps its unspent reads, so the room
  coming back is never measured again — the nine-hour silence returns.

history:
  Measured on the home machine 2026-08-12. A rebuild at 00:54:23 (the
  speaker left the group and was walked back in) armed a settle round;
  playback stopped around 00:57 and the round died against its gates
  with all five reads unspent. Nothing armed another, because a round
  could only be born at a build. The room stayed 55-60 ms out for the
  next nine hours, through a park, a wake and two mornings of periodic
  checks, and only came right when it was finally given six
  uninterrupted minutes — 202 -> 143, residual 56 ms -> 3 ms.

  The fix has two halves and this mutant removes the quiet one. Zeroing
  the reads is what makes a dead round LOOK dead; the resume road reads
  that pulse to tell a corpse from a live round. Drop it and the resume
  guard silently stops firing while every log line still looks right —
  which is the same shape as the bug it replaced. This exact slip was
  made once while writing the fix, and its test caught it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
                  _settleReadsLeft = 0;
                  settleFixTimer.stop();
                  console.log("[ARP] sync: settle gave up its window — "

replace:
                  settleFixTimer.stop();
                  console.log("[ARP] sync: settle gave up its window — "

expect:
  Killed by tst_syncengine.qml
  test_a_room_that_comes_back_unconfirmed_gets_a_second_round: the dead
  round still reports five reads left, the resume guard refuses, and the
  fresh round's gate-retry budget never returns to ten.
